# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# A stray copy named `env` (no dot) slips past the patterns above and carries
# the same live keys. Ignore it too rather than rely on nobody running `git add .`.
/env

# Runtime artefacts (T-008)
# ⚠️ ANCHORED with a leading slash — these must match ONLY the runtime
# directories at the repo root. Unanchored, `data/` also matched the source
# package `src/researchgpt/data/`, so the entire Phase 2 data layer (chunker,
# embeddings, vectorstore, bm25_index, metadata_db — including two ★
# critical-path tasks) was silently excluded from the first commit. Found
# 2026-08-26. Never un-anchor these.
/data/
/outputs/

# Review decks (T-008)
*.pptx

# Trained-model archives downloaded from Kaggle (T-303, T-332).
# The verifier checkpoint alone is a 496 MB zip. It arrives at the repo root
# from the browser, where nothing was ignoring it — `git add -A` would have
# committed half a gigabyte of weights. Weights are reproducible from the
# notebook; the repo holds the code that makes them, not the artefacts.
# Unzip them into /data/models/ (already ignored) and delete the archive.
*.zip
*.safetensors
*.onnx

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage

# Local caches and model weights
.cache/
.huggingface/
*.onnx

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Claude local permission log (machine-specific)
.claude/settings.local.json

# T-212/T-213 gathered pool cache (large, regenerable)
eval/cache/

# T-410 metrics write-up. Untracked on purpose (requested 2026-08-29): it is a
# working report over run artefacts that live in the gitignored outputs/, so it
# is regenerable from `python -m researchgpt.eval.run_metrics` and would
# otherwise churn on every run.
eval/metrics_evaluated.md

# Phase 6 frontend. node_modules is 32 packages of build tooling; dist/ is
# generated by `npm run build`. Neither belongs in the repo.
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
